---- the credential ----
rpId          example.com
credentialId  4ae6262861c2429e9f87a454397fde93e63afe216a775ccb682d631d47ab809e
publicKey     60fed4ba255a9d31c961eb74c6356d68…  (64 bytes, X||Y)
kdfSalt       7ed8b2dc4d8643466c9be5a58012a28d
nonce         74f644c9da73926fc8512637
sealedKey     251086a8a5a3daabd8b4a5c441a412ec…  (48 bytes = 32 key + 16 tag)

the site stores : credentialId + publicKey, nothing else
never leaves you: the private key, even in encrypted form

---- signing a login challenge ----
signature     f31c959c8624b563814f7976dfec3ab7…  (64 bytes, r||s)
server verify true  (want true)

---- the failures that matter ----
wrong password        -> 0 bytes (want 0)
key moved to new rpId -> 0 bytes (want 0)
one flipped bit       -> 0 bytes (want 0)
replay, new challenge -> false (want false)
replay, new origin    -> false (want false)

---- real generation (random, so only properties are printed) ----
generated             true (want true)
keys differ           true (want true)
salts differ          true (want true)
nonces differ         true (want true)
credential ids differ true (want true)
signs and verifies    true (want true)
wrong key rejects     false (want false)
